WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
ano toki umareta no

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
あのとき生まれたの

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
I'll softly give you my thoughts

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
watashi no omoi sotto ageru

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
私の想いそっとあげる

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
That were born at that moment

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
shinjite ite

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
信じていて

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
Please believe in them

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
deatta hi kara

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
出逢った日から

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
Since the day when we met

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
hajimete no kimochi megutteru

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
初めての気持ち巡ってる

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
For the first time, I have these feelings, and they go around

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
honto no egao hoshii nante

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
ホントの笑顔ほしいなんて

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
I want your true smile

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
anata ga oshiete kureta sorao

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
あなたが教えてくれた空を

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
I embrace the sky

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
dakishimete yume o miru

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
抱きしめて夢をみる

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
That you told me about and dream

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
tooi keredo・・・

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
遠いけれど・・・

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
It's faraway, but...

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
atatakai hikari no kakera

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
あたたかい光のかけら

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
The fragments of warm light

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
kizutsuita hane ni inochi o kureta no

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
傷ついた羽根に命をくれたの

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
Gave life to my wounded wings

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
fureta toki umareta

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
触れたとき生まれた

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
Born at the moment when we touched

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
tsuyoi watashi no soba ni

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
強い私のそばに

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
Next to me, who is strong

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
mamoraretai watashi ga nemutte ita no

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
守られたいわたしが眠っていたの

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
The me who wants to be protected was asleep

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
sou unmei kaerareru ne

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
そう運命変えられるね

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
That's right, destiny can be changed

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
futari no koi mezamesasete・・・

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
ふたりの恋目覚めさせて・・・

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
Let our love awaken...

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:29.940
{last frame of OP}

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.440
I wonder if I can get worker's compensation insurance if I get economy class syndrome?

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.450
The inside of the car stinks from lunch.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.120
Samidare Apartment, huh?

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.210
Right, rain in May, early summer rain.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.210
Note: Samidare - Early summer rain.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.540
It's a fitting name.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.540
Sounds like an unlucky place to be in the month of May.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.460
The one from last night?

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.920
That guy looks completely drained of energy. {TLC - drained of energy -> worn out maybe, other one doesn't sound natural}

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.980
Women become wild as soon as the first piece of clothing comes off.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.640
Wild in the early summer rain.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.640
Note: A play on the words Samidare and midareru.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.190
So, Murasaki was in Tokyo?

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.090
Yes.

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.630
Tokyo is a place that can fill you with disgust,

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:15.240
but it is also said to be a high-class place.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.830
Her experiences from living there will be helpful in some way.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.370
And would this <i>helpful </i>experience be needed for a woman of the Inner Sanctuary?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:28.800
Have you ever sympathized with the women of the Inner Sanctuary before?

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.470
What can I do for someone whom I was taught not to sympathize with?

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:39.250
So even you, who knows the outside world, can say that.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.720
What are you asking of me, when I don't even know how it feels to be born cursed?

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.850
I wonder what Murasaki is thinking?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.900
She's only seven years old.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.210
You're right.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.450
Seven years old...

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.610
That's right.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.620
Did you forget?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:02.170
Up until she was seven, she had lived in God's residence.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.290
If she were in society, it'd be time for the obi ceremony.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.590
Society has nothing to do with the Kuhouins.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.210
You're right.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:13.550
Before Murasaki had even turned seven, she had already tied her own obi.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.050
I had thought that was proper etiquette.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.060
You're exactly right.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.170
The tea got cold.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.310
I'm sorry.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.740
The room is cold, too.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:36.230
Eighth Episode 「Taking Care of Oneself and Cowardice」

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.020
This is just terrible.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.280
Today's bread is good.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.990
Really?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.120
Isn't it too sweet?

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.410
It certainly is sweet.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.160
I like it.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.850
I like it too.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.870
Everyone gets their own meals starting tomorrow, okay?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.980
Come on, isn't it lonely?

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.590
Then bring your own meals.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.420
I chipped my tooth.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.420
With bread?

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.140
That's awful. Are you getting old, Yamie?

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.640
A bad premonition right in the morning.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:07.390
Speaking of this month's 15th, it's Shichi-Go-San, isn't it?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.990
Hey, wait, it's almost Shichi-Go-San!

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.040
Shichi-Go-San?

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.880
You're seven, right, Murasaki-chan?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.400
Yeah.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.030
We've got to celebrate, then.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:17.900
Celebrate?

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.950
Shichi-Go-San is when you celebrate that you're 3, 5 or 7 years old.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.950
Note: Shichi-Go-San = 7-5-3

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:27.140
You're not wrong, but that's a crude explanation.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.710
So, Shichi-Go-San is on the 15th of November.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.130
Hey, let's all go to a temple and celebrate Shichi-Go-San.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:36.550
Was there a temple in this area, though?

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.630
There is.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.130
Hanazono Shrine.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.470
It's near the place where detective Bogey was killed in the line of duty.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.660
Bogey?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.240
You know, the one in "Roar at the Sun!"

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:48.220
He got shot in the stomach and died after yelling "What the hell is this?" when he looked at his blood.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.200
Isn't that Jeans?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:55.210
After he got shot, he crawled to the elevator, but then he got cut off and died.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.240
That's Detective Rugger.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.620
Was it?

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.560
What do you do to celebrate?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.050
Shinkurou-kun will buy you anything.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.310
Wai-

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.640
A high school student living by himself.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.330
That woman is always there.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.630
Yeah, she's Benika's subordinate.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.730
Inuzuka Yayoi.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.130
We should switch soon, or they'll figure us out.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.120
Yeah.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.880
Let's change cars for now.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.300
Hey.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.290
Did you find something about the Kuhouins yet?

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.270
Give me some more time.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.410
It looks like they aren't just your everyday rich people.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.310
Really?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.270
There's something strange about that household.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.640
Are they that troublesome?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.700
Yeah.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.260
I see.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:45.860
Oh yeah, November 15th is Shichi-Go-San, right?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:46.950
Shichi-Go-San?

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.620
Hey, what did you do for your Shichi-Go-San, Ginko?

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.460
Why?

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:55.340
I was wondering what girls do on Shichi-Go-San.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:56.650
Like I said, why?

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:58.190
Because it's coming up soon.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.380
This is an expensive looking kimono.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:08.120
We'll go visit Hanazono Shrine, take some commemorative pictures,

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:11.670
buy some chitose candy and then go eat out with everyone!

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:14.140
And it'll <i>all </i>be on Shinkurou.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:19.770
But before that, let's put some shadow on her face and dye her lips blood red.

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.360
That's makeup, right?

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:32.080
It's just too surprising to see you have these colors, Yamie-san.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.580
I may use them depending on the person.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.330
Like what kind of person?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.780
Like an old man who likes little girls.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.010
We won't do anything to stand out, and there'll also be a bunch of kids around.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.400
And what would you do if something were to happen to her?

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.800
That's true, but,

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:52.950
Shichi-Go-San is a once in a lifetime day for Murasaki.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.430
I understand, but...

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.840
We can walk while encircling her.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.250
That'll make you stand out more.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.880
Then...

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.990
I'll report this to Benika-sama and get her thoughts on it.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.650
I see.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.200
I think it's fine.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.450
I understand, but it'll be a good memory for her.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.960
Could you at least make them go to a small shrine, then?

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.250
There are too many people at Hanazono Shrine, and if something happens...

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.130
Yes... Yes...

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:27.380
That place should be fine, as it's in front of the station, after all.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.580
Right.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:31.200
Then make sure not to stand out.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.140
Yes, yes, yes.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.460
They said it's Shichi-Go-San.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.040
Do you have children?

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.150
Boys? Girls?

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.710
It's okay if you go to the shrine in front of the station.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.070
In front of the station?

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.170
There was one there?

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.650
Shinkurou!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.560
What do you think? Did I become a mature woman?

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.830
Yeah, it's great. I almost didn't recognize you.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:01.320
Come on, let's go.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.700
It's been a while since I've gone to the Hanazono Shrine.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.970
Let's eat some candy apples, okay, Murasaki-chan?

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.690
We've got to go where detective Bogey was killed, too.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.010
This is going to be fun!

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:10.930
Excuse me.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:15.350
There's been a slight change.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.760
Miss, could I have a potato salad too?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.260
Sure thing, here you go.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.590
A fried chicken bento and a mixed fried bento.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.860
A potato salad, too.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.550
Ah, we only have tuna salad.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:25.460
Really?

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.440
Ah, what should I do?

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.300
Perfect, let me ask him.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:32.530
Sorry about that.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.200
Hello? Perfect timing.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.050
About your salad, the potato- What?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.590
They sure are daring.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.380
Don't tell me, is that it?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.630
It's small.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.350
So this is a shrine?

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:55.140
There aren't going to be any shop stands for sure.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:57.480
Looks like nothing will happen, either.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.170
Murasaki-chan.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:02.590
Let's take a picture first. What's 1+1?

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:05.110
2!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:18.120
What's wrong?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.890
What are those things, Shinkurou?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.630
Ah, they're guardian lion-dogs.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.010
Lion-dogs?

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:28.080
Yeah.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.340
I think it's supposed to be a dog.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.180
Do you know anything?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:33.870
Don't you like dogs?

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:36.330
I like cats.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.350
Yayoi-san.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.520
I've never had a pet before.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.230
I'm not sure.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.090
You don't know?

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.520
Ah, I got it!

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.830
It's that! You know, they're all over Okinawa.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:49.690
Um, shi... shi... shikuwasa!

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:53.010
They say that if you put it in front of your house, bad things won't be able to get in!

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:55.340
Isn't that a Shisa?

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.170
Is it?

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:58.830
Shikuwasa is a fruit, the sour one.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.350
Isn't Shisa a salad?

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.420
That's Caesar salad.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.060
What's umibudou, then?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:10.050
I see, they have scary faces, but they're actually good guys.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:08.660
Isn't it when you get drunk from sea water?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:08.660
Note: umibudou = sea grapes, but umi = sea and budou = wine.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.050
Forget it.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:15.000
Why are there two?

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:17.290
Siblings?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:21.680
They're not Shisa, right?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:25.090
How are you supposed to formally pray, again?

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.440
First, you put in your offering, ring the bell,

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.170
bow twice, and then clap twice.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:35.110
You then put your hands together to pray and finish it off with another bow.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.610
As expected from an old woman.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.030
It's common sense.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.210
All right, I did it.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.740
You have to bow one more time at the end.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:54.880
Ah, that's right.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.220
Hey, hey!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.760
It says this place is famous for improving your luck with money and gambling!

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:02.520
What?

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.850
Damn, I have to splurge on the offering in preparation for next year.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:11.110
Come true! Please come true!

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:12.780
God is with me!

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.090
I got a slightly good fortune.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.280
How unlucky.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:21.580
I can't read it, Shinkurou. What's written on it?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.000
Bad fortune?

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.520
What does that mean?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.530
Is something wrong?

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:35.050
Ah, no...

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:39.590
It means that things aren't going well now, but <i>lots </i>of good things will happen later.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.600
I see, so there'll be a lot of good things later.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.080
Yep.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.640
Oh yeah, let's buy a charm, Murasaki.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:53.840
When a person keeps a charm by their side, it'll protect that person from evil.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.100
Which one do you like?

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:57.190
I like that one.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:58.860
That one?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:11:59.950
The pink one.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:03.890
You're sure you want this one?

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.010
Yeah.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:06.950
Oh well.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:08.700
Can I have this one, please?

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.420
Yes.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:12.490
You're sure going all out.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.670
It's a once in a lifetime celebration for Murasaki-chan, after all.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:18.170
I borrowed it from a junior at my university.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:21.150
I'm taking a picture now.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.560
1+1 is?

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:27.370
2!

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.860
Ah, I closed my eyes!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.300
What are you doing?

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:35.400
The timer is too long.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.980
She's like a captured alien!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.160
You're right.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.660
Let's take a normal picture.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:12:59.030
Sorry for the wait.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:00.180
Who ordered beer?

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.330
Ah, right here!

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.480
The shikuwasa is over here.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.140
Right.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.810
So shikuwasa <i>was </i>a fruit.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.700
Just like I said, right?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.560
The guardian lion-dogs are relatives of the Shisa.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.050
I'm not even sure anymore, so let's forget about that.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:17.270
Anyway, let's have a toast.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:23.310
Well then, to Murasaki's Shichi-Go-San and bright future, cheers!

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:25.400
Cheers!

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.140
This is good!

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.700
Drinking at places like this sometimes is nice.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:33.920
It's good.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:36.340
That shrine was great, too.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:37.900
We could take our time.

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.240
Our luck with money went up, too.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:42.420
It's unfortunate that they didn't sell chitose candy, though.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.850
But Shinkurou bought this for me.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:48.100
I can have peace of mind if I hold onto this while Shinkurou is away.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:52.140
It's about time you came to me.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:54.320
Forgive me.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:59.650
Renjou, do you still have feelings for Souju or not?

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:01.900
None.

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:07.960
Murasaki is in a position where she must be hidden from society.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:11.980
Furthermore, our affairs must not be leaked out somewhere.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:16.160
If anything were to happen, it will not reach the public.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.050
You need not worry on this matter.

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:22.520
You cannot be hesitant when taking out the stains in clothing.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:23.130
Ryuuji.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.180
I am handling it.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.820
However,

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:33.560
I will be careful from now on and settle this so that no one outside may even suspect it.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.640
Why?

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:38.110
I can see a small seam coming apart on you, father. {guessing it's related to line 273}

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:43.820
You're being rude, speaking to your father like that, Ryuuji.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.270
It's not like you're in a stalemate or the clock has stopped after all this time, right? {chess terms}

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:49.210
I have found where she is.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.400
I see.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:57.000
However, there is no need to trouble yourself anymore, father.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:01.670
Please prepare the Inner Sanctuary and wait.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.090
You...

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:08.010
Murasaki is the last woman left to us.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.550
I will treat her with the utmost care.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.220
Bye, now.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.070
Take care on your way home.

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:24.330
Where are you two going?

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.180
Shinjuku.

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:26.990
We didn't drink enough.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:29.370
I'd come with you if I could drink beer.

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.690
You can once you're older.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:34.080
I'll show you to a bunch of good shops then.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:36.790
I'll count on you when the time comes, then.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:40.800
Today was a good day.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:42.440
Shichi-Go-San was fun.

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:43.790
That's great.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:46.770
Oh yeah, there was something I wanted to ask you, Shinkurou.

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:47.220
What?

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.710
Do you like women with big breasts?

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.650
Tamaki-san again?

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:54.490
Yeah.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.810
She said that men like women with breasts as big as cow udders.{TLC - she doesn't say udders, just says "breasts as big as a cow"}

00:15:57.810 --> 00:15:59.580
I wonder about that.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.810
My mother's breasts were big,

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.700
so I think I'll become like her some day.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.980
It'll take a long time, though.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:11.380
It's unfortunate, but I can't please you as I am now.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.780
P-Please me?

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.620
It's frustrating.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:19.210
I'm really frustrated that I'm a child.

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:23.210
I can't say much to you and I can't do much for you either.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.840
You taught me a lot of things.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.650
Like the bath house, the school, and the shrine.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:34.050
You showed me a lot of things I didn't know about.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:38.190
I want to grow up quickly for your sake.

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:41.270
I want to quickly become a mature woman that's befitting of you.

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.630
You're good enough.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.690
You're good enough the way you are now.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.130
The way I am now?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.180
Yeah.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.610
I like the way you are now.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.620
I see.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.200
I'll do what I can now, then.

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.930
I'll do it all properly.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:58.870
Okay.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.780
It's cold outside.

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:02.160
Let's go home quickly.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.480
Okay.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.570
So it <i>is</i> true that you can become accustomed to living anywhere.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:11.120
I want to always be with you here, just like I am now.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.240
Are you okay with this small room?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:16.860
Yeah, I want to know about a lot of things.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:19.480
Like stories from when you were young.

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.070
You don't need to know those.

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:22.520
Yuuno knows them, though.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.730
Things that will happen from now on are enough.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.700
Forget about the past.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:29.070
Now is the most fun.

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:33.170
Really? You're happy with me here?

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:34.710
Yeah, I'm happy.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:36.920
I see, you're happy!

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:40.000
Come on, I'm going to turn the lights off, so let's sleep.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.500
Okay.

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:43.500
Good night.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.580
Good night.

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:52.200
Good morning, Shinkurou-san.

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.310
Good morning.

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.930
It's cold, isn't it?

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.320
Yeah, winter's here already.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.460
Is Murasaki-chan doing well?

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.420
Yeah.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.900
We went to a nearby shrine to celebrate Shichi-Go-San.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.350
Is that so?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:09.280
If you had told me, I could have helped her put her kimono on.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:13.180
Tamaki-san did it, surprisingly.

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.780
That's shocking beyond belief.

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:19.170
She seems to have played with kimonos before.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.450
So that's how it is?

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.650
What is it?

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:26.460
You don't need to know.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:32.360
I can't believe it. That's a dangerous apartment.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.550
Murakami Ginko

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.550
Kurenai

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.550
「Come. Ginko」

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:45.150
Is this real?

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.100
No doubt about it.

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:48.530
But...

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.860
There is no girl named Murasaki in the Kuhouin family.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.740
Then whose child is Murasaki?

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:55.690
I don't know.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:58.290
Juuzawa Benika may be lying,

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.240
or perhaps there's some huge conspiracy.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.650
It's certain that she's a rich girl, though.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.750
Like, her attitude towards life, and her manners.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:08.180
I understand, but...

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.660
A small girl like her can't lie.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.620
She may just not know it herself.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:17.050
The Kuhouins are plutocratic world leaders.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:19.280
They're a household that would probably do anything.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:21.510
That can't be.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.970
They're not a group you could possibly oppose.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:29.030
They may even make it as if you've never existed.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:35.880
By the way, the current head of the family is Kuhouin Renjou.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:39.110
And that person has two male children.

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:40.490
Male?

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.250
I am Kuhouin Murasaki.

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:51.090
How about you ask Juuzawa Benika?

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:54.790
Shinkurou?

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.710
She isn't lying.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.750
There must be some extenuating circumstances.

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:18.280
Something...

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:21.830
Ah, excuse me. Are you from this apartment?

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:22.830
Yes.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:26.330
There's a small girl here, right?

00:20:28.510 --> 00:20:31.210
There is one, isn't there? A seven year old girl.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.120
Murasaki!

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:05.000
The Kuhouins?

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.590
You're certain?

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.870
I see, it was quicker than I imagined.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.780
Please make a quick decision.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:14.920
I'll be there soon.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:19.880
Murasaki?!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:22.050
Ah, welcome back, Shinkurou.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:30.560
Murasaki...

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:35.040
What's wrong? Did you want to see me so much that you ran?

00:21:37.090 --> 00:21:40.120
Shinkurou? What's wrong?

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:44.820
Murasaki, we can't stay here anymore.

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:46.490
What?

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:50.120
The Kuhouins found this place.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:53.010
We can't stay here anymore.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.370
No, am I going back home?

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:57.920
No, you don't want to go back, right?

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:01.420
I don't want to go back! I don't want to go back to the Kuhouins!

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:11.760
There is no girl named Murasaki in the Kuhouin family.

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:19.650
Kurenai-san.

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:21.570
Benika-sama is coming to pick you up.

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:26.450
I will be standing on guard out front.

